  "description": "Category profile architecture@1: what a model element is, for the model reading, whatever the family a modeller picked. Each category names its French label, the words people use for it (synonyms) and the clues that recognise it: IFC classes, predefined types, type-name patterns, and geometric conditions (exterior side, sill, height, width, thickness, orientation). The first matching category by priority wins; an element matching none stays 'element (IFC class)'; a category marked ignore is counted, not read. Recognising a category is a reading, never a fact admitted into the Anatomy. An agency may add categories and synonyms through a local file kept outside the repository; that file is add-only.",
  "profile": {
    "id": "architecture@1",
    "governs": "model reading element categories and the words of designations",
    "agency_file": {
      "environment_variable": "PANTHEON_CATEGORY_OVERLAY",
      "registry_kind": "vocabulary_overlay",
      "extends": "architecture_category_profile",
      "rules": [
        "add-only: an id declared by this registry cannot be redeclared, changed or deprecated",
        "ids follow naming_rules.id_pattern",
        "status is active or candidate",
        "an unreadable or invalid file makes the vocabulary unavailable instead of being ignored"
      ]
    }
  },
  "naming_rules": {
    "id_pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{1,39}$",
    "max_agency_entries": 200
  },
